WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.741 --> 00:00:02.843
&gt;&gt; Chris: DAVID SPUNT,

00:00:02.877 --> 00:00:03.913
REPORTING FROM BRIDGEWATER,

00:00:03.947 --> 00:00:05.763
NEW JERSEY, DAVID, THANK YOU.

00:00:05.798 --> 00:00:08.397
JOINING US NOW, SECRETARY OF THE

00:00:08.399 --> 00:00:09.628
SIDE, TREASURY, STEVEN MNUCHIN.

00:00:09.662 --> 00:00:10.995
ESTHER SECRETARY, WELCOME BACK

00:00:11.029 --> 00:00:11.904
TO "FOX NEWS SUNDAY."

00:00:11.939 --> 00:00:13.003
&gt;&gt; Secretary Mnuchin:

00:00:13.005 --> 00:00:14.847
THANK YOU, IT’S GOOD TO BE WITH

00:00:14.881 --> 00:00:15.281
YOU.

00:00:15.315 --> 00:00:16.535
&gt;&gt; Chris: HOUSE DEMOCRATS

00:00:16.536 --> 00:00:18.625
PASSED THEIR RELIEF BILL BACK IN

00:00:18.659 --> 00:00:21.276
MAY, FULLY TWO MONTHS AGO, BUT

00:00:21.310 --> 00:00:22.952
HERE WE ARE THE LAST WEEK IN

00:00:22.954 --> 00:00:25.808
JULY AND THE WHITE HOUSE AND

00:00:25.809 --> 00:00:27.629
SENATE REPUBLICANS STILL CAN’T

00:00:27.631 --> 00:00:30.492
AGREE ON JUST A G.O.P. PACKAGE.

00:00:30.526 --> 00:00:32.259
MEANWHILE, A FEDERAL BAN ON

00:00:32.293 --> 00:00:34.263
EVICTIONS RAN OUT YESTERDAY,

00:00:34.264 --> 00:00:35.605
FEDERAL UNEMPLOYMENT BENEFITS

00:00:35.606 --> 00:00:39.026
RUN OUT ON FRIDAY IN THE LAST

00:00:39.061 --> 00:00:40.737
CHECKS OF ALREADY GOT OUT AND

00:00:40.739 --> 00:00:41.540
THE PAYROLL PROTECTION PROGRAM

00:00:41.575 --> 00:00:44.218
FOR BUSINESSES IS RUNNING OUT

00:00:44.219 --> 00:00:46.055
EARLY NEXT MONTH.

00:00:46.090 --> 00:00:47.716
HERE IS SENATE DEMOCRATIC LEADER

00:00:47.750 --> 00:00:48.355
CHUCK SCHUMER.

00:00:48.356 --> 00:00:51.344
&gt;&gt; THEY HAVE BEEN SO DIVIDED, SO

00:00:51.346 --> 00:00:52.716
DISORGANIZED, SO UNPREPARED,

00:00:52.751 --> 00:00:54.414
THAT THEY HAVE STRUGGLED TO EVEN

00:00:54.415 --> 00:00:56.036
DRAFT A PARTISAN PROPOSAL WITHIN

00:00:56.038 --> 00:00:58.671
THEIR OWN CONFERENCE.

00:00:58.672 --> 00:01:01.004
THEY CAN’T COME TOGETHER.

00:01:01.039 --> 00:01:03.247
&gt;&gt; Chris: WON’T MILLIONS OF

00:01:03.248 --> 00:01:04.292
AMERICANS, AND MILLIONS OF

00:01:04.327 --> 00:01:06.718
BUSINESSES, PAY THE PRICE,

00:01:06.720 --> 00:01:08.278
BECAUSE THE WHITE HOUSE AND

00:01:08.313 --> 00:01:10.285
SENATE REPUBLICANS CAN’T GET

00:01:10.319 --> 00:01:11.114
YOUR ACT TOGETHER?

00:01:11.149 --> 00:01:12.787
&gt;&gt; Secretary Mnuchin: LET ME

00:01:12.789 --> 00:01:13.988
SAY, I THINK THAT’S UNFAIR

00:01:13.989 --> 00:01:14.928
CHARACTERIZATION.

00:01:14.930 --> 00:01:17.477
THE ADMINISTRATION AND THE

00:01:17.511 --> 00:01:18.387
SENATE REPUBLICANS ARE

00:01:18.389 --> 00:01:20.155
COMPLETELY ON THE SAME PAGE.

00:01:20.189 --> 00:01:22.685
MARK MEADOWS AND I WERE UP

00:01:22.686 --> 00:01:23.751
YESTERDAY JUST WORKING ON

00:01:23.752 --> 00:01:24.752
TECHNICAL ISSUES IN THE DRAFTS.

00:01:24.753 --> 00:01:26.420
IF WE HAVE PREVIOUSLY AGREED ON

00:01:26.421 --> 00:01:28.019
ALL THESE ISSUES EARLIER IN THE

00:01:28.053 --> 00:01:28.687
WEEK.

00:01:28.721 --> 00:01:31.831
WE WANT TO MOVE FORWARD QUICKLY.

00:01:31.832 --> 00:01:33.350
THE BILL WILL BE INTRODUCED

00:01:33.351 --> 00:01:34.960
MONDAY AND WE ARE PREPARED TO

00:01:34.962 --> 00:01:36.053
ACT QUICKLY.

00:01:36.054 --> 00:01:37.831
THIS IS ALL ABOUT KIDS AND JOBS.

00:01:37.865 --> 00:01:39.967
THIS IS OUR FOCUS AND WE WANT TO

00:01:40.001 --> 00:01:41.394
MAKE SURE SOMETHING GETS PASSED

00:01:41.395 --> 00:01:42.768
QUICKLY SO THAT WE DEAL WITH THE

00:01:42.802 --> 00:01:44.925
UNEMPLOYMENT AT ALL THE OTHER

00:01:44.927 --> 00:01:46.462
ISSUES, PAYCHECK PROTECTION

00:01:46.496 --> 00:01:49.284
PLAN, TAX CREDITS TO REHIRE

00:01:49.285 --> 00:01:51.659
PEOPLE AND MONEY FOR SCHOOLS.

00:01:51.660 --> 00:01:53.089
&gt;&gt; Chris: BUT MR. SECRETARY,

00:01:53.091 --> 00:01:54.709
THE PLAN WAS SUPPOSED TO BE

00:01:54.710 --> 00:01:56.540
ANNOUNCED ON WEDNESDAY, THEN

00:01:56.542 --> 00:01:57.881
THURSDAY, NOW IT’S NEXT WEEK.

00:01:57.882 --> 00:01:59.792
AND IT’S TWO MONTHS AFTER THE

00:01:59.793 --> 00:02:01.040
DEMOCRATS CAME UP WITH THEIR

00:02:01.041 --> 00:02:03.877
PLAN AND NOW YOU’RE GOING TO

00:02:03.878 --> 00:02:05.875
HAVE TO START NEGOTIATING WITH

00:02:05.910 --> 00:02:07.891
DEMOCRATS NOW THAT YOU HAVE A

00:02:07.925 --> 00:02:09.629
REPUBLICAN PLAN, SENATE MAJORITY

00:02:09.663 --> 00:02:11.765
LEADER MITCH McCONNELL SAID

00:02:11.767 --> 00:02:13.256
FRIDAY HOPEFULLY WE CAN COME

00:02:13.257 --> 00:02:16.285
TOGETHER BEHIND SOME PACKAGE WE

00:02:16.286 --> 00:02:18.339
CAN AGREE ON IN THE NEXT FEW

00:02:18.374 --> 00:02:20.197
WEEKS AND HERE’S WHITE HOUSE

00:02:20.198 --> 00:02:21.832
CHIEF OF STAFF MARK MEADOWS.

00:02:21.834 --> 00:02:24.118
&gt;&gt; WE ARE TRYING TO MAKE SURE

00:02:24.153 --> 00:02:26.304
THAT WE GET THE IMMEDIATE NEEDS

00:02:26.305 --> 00:02:27.544
FIRST AND THEN CONTINUE TO

00:02:27.545 --> 00:02:28.830
NEGOTIATE PERHAPS THROUGHOUT

00:02:28.832 --> 00:02:31.507
MOST OF AUGUST UNTIL WE GET

00:02:31.541 --> 00:02:32.531
SOMETHING FINISHED.

00:02:32.565 --> 00:02:35.252
&gt;&gt; Chris: SO DO YOU HAVE A

00:02:35.253 --> 00:02:38.520
G.O.P. PLAN THAT WILL BE

00:02:38.521 --> 00:02:40.803
ANNOUNCED TOMORROW, AND THEN,

00:02:40.804 --> 00:02:42.414
WHAT ARE LAID-OFF WORKERS AND

00:02:42.448 --> 00:02:43.590
WATER STRUGGLING BUSINESSES

00:02:43.591 --> 00:02:45.219
SUPPOSED TO DO WHILE YOU SPEND,

00:02:45.220 --> 00:02:48.314
AS THE WHITE HOUSE CHIEF OF

00:02:48.315 --> 00:02:50.737
STAFF JUST SAID UNTIL SOMETIME

00:02:50.738 --> 00:02:51.984
IN AUGUST NEGOTIATING WITH

00:02:51.985 --> 00:02:52.229
DEMOCRATS?

00:02:52.230 --> 00:02:53.099
&gt;&gt; Secretary Mnuchin: LET ME

00:02:53.100 --> 00:02:54.826
FIRST SAY WE DO HAVE AN ENTIRE

00:02:54.827 --> 00:02:57.201
PLAN, IT’S A TRILLION DOLLARS

00:02:57.236 --> 00:02:58.877
AND LET ME JUST REMIND EVERYBODY

00:02:58.911 --> 00:03:00.781
THAT OF THE $3 TRILLION WITH

00:03:00.782 --> 00:03:02.361
ALREADY FAST, WE HAVE ABOUT A

00:03:02.362 --> 00:03:04.124
TRILLION TO A TRILLION AND A

00:03:04.125 --> 00:03:05.545
HALF STILL LEFT TO PUT INTO THE

00:03:05.546 --> 00:03:08.367
ECONOMY SO THESE ARE VERY, VERY

00:03:08.402 --> 00:03:09.806
LARGE AMOUNT OF MONEY, WORKING

00:03:09.840 --> 00:03:11.894
WITH CONGRESS TO SUPPORT THIS

00:03:11.896 --> 00:03:13.613
AND WHAT MARK MEADOWS WAS SAYING

00:03:13.614 --> 00:03:15.211
IS THAT WITHIN THE TRILLION

00:03:15.245 --> 00:03:16.865
DOLLAR PACKAGE, THERE ARE

00:03:16.900 --> 00:03:18.789
CERTAIN THINGS THAT HAVE TIME

00:03:18.790 --> 00:03:20.483
FRAMES THAT ARE BIGGER PRIORITY,

00:03:20.485 --> 00:03:21.794
SO WE COULD LOOK AT DOING AN

00:03:21.829 --> 00:03:24.647
ENTIRE DEAL, WE COULD ALSO LOOK

00:03:24.649 --> 00:03:26.691
AT DOING PARTS, SO OBVIOUSLY THE

00:03:26.725 --> 00:03:28.627
MOST PRESSING ISSUES ARE THE

00:03:28.628 --> 00:03:29.967
FACT THAT WE HAVE UNEMPLOYMENT

00:03:30.001 --> 00:03:30.542
INSURANCE RUNNING OUT.

00:03:30.576 --> 00:03:32.887
WE NEED TO MAKE SURE THAT WE

00:03:32.889 --> 00:03:35.152
DON’T HAVE FRIVOLOUS LAWSUITS

00:03:35.153 --> 00:03:36.434
FOR SCHOOLS AND UNIVERSITIES.

00:03:36.469 --> 00:03:37.987
WE WANT TO MAKE SURE WITH THE

00:03:38.021 --> 00:03:39.204
EXPIRING UNEMPLOYMENT INSURANCE

00:03:39.206 --> 00:03:40.717
WE HAVE THE TECHNICAL FIX SO

00:03:40.751 --> 00:03:43.313
PEOPLE DON’T GET PAID MORE TO

00:03:43.347 --> 00:03:45.330
STAY HOME THAN THEY DO TO WORK

00:03:45.364 --> 00:03:47.118
AND WE CAN MOVE VERY QUICKLY

00:03:47.152 --> 00:03:48.253
WITH THE DEMOCRATS ON THESE

00:03:48.254 --> 00:03:48.856
ISSUES.

00:03:48.857 --> 00:03:51.083
WE’VE MOVED QUICKLY BEFORE AND I

00:03:51.117 --> 00:03:52.683
SEE NO REASON WHY WE CAN MOVE

00:03:52.717 --> 00:03:54.897
QUICKLY AGAIN AND IF THERE ARE

00:03:54.931 --> 00:03:57.728
ISSUES THAT TAKE LONGER, WE WILL

00:03:57.729 --> 00:03:59.760
DEAL WITH THOSE AS WELL.

00:03:59.794 --> 00:04:00.993
&gt;&gt; Chris: BUT MR. SECRETARY,

00:04:01.027 --> 00:04:02.505
YOU KNOW, BECAUSE NANCY PELOSI

00:04:02.506 --> 00:04:04.444
HAS MADE VERY CLEAR, SHE’S NOT

00:04:04.445 --> 00:04:06.625
GOING TO AGREE TO A PIECEMEAL

00:04:06.627 --> 00:04:08.344
PLAN BECAUSE THE THINGS THAT YOU

00:04:08.345 --> 00:04:09.263
WANT IMMEDIATELY OTHER THINGS

00:04:09.297 --> 00:04:11.368
THAT YOU WANT AND THERE ARE

00:04:11.403 --> 00:04:13.227
THINGS THEY WANT AND ARE NOT

00:04:13.261 --> 00:04:15.555
GOING TO AGREE TO SOME THINGS

00:04:15.589 --> 00:04:18.204
UNTIL EVERYTHING IS AGREED TO.

00:04:18.205 --> 00:04:20.389
LET’S FOCUS, IF WE CAN,

00:04:20.423 --> 00:04:22.015
SPECIFICALLY ON THE UNEMPLOYMENT

00:04:22.049 --> 00:04:24.094
BENEFITS, BECAUSE THAT SEEMS TO

00:04:24.095 --> 00:04:26.128
BE THE BIG HOLDUP, CERTAINLY

00:04:26.129 --> 00:04:27.159
AMONG REPUBLICANS.

00:04:27.193 --> 00:04:29.248
THE PLAN THAT IS JUST RUNNING

00:04:29.249 --> 00:04:31.977
OUT NOW PROVIDED A FEDERAL

00:04:31.979 --> 00:04:34.567
EMPLOYMENT BENEFIT ON TOP OF

00:04:34.568 --> 00:04:37.091
STATE UNEMPLOYMENT BENEFITS,

00:04:37.092 --> 00:04:40.582
FEDERAL BENEFIT OF $600 A WEEK.

00:04:40.616 --> 00:04:41.858
YOU’RE SAYING THAT’S TOO MUCH.

00:04:41.859 --> 00:04:44.160
HOW MUCH DO YOU PLAN TO REDUCE

00:04:44.161 --> 00:04:45.397
IT AND WHY?

00:04:45.431 --> 00:04:47.026
&gt;&gt; Secretary Mnuchin: WELL,

00:04:47.027 --> 00:04:48.140
CHRIS, JUST REMEMBER, WHEN WE

00:04:48.175 --> 00:04:50.441
DID THE LAST PLAN -- AND LET ME

00:04:50.442 --> 00:04:51.832
SAY, WHEN YOU TALK ABOUT

00:04:51.867 --> 00:04:53.508
PIECEMEAL, THIS WILL BE THE

00:04:53.510 --> 00:04:55.231
FIFTH SET OF LEGISLATION, SO

00:04:55.233 --> 00:04:56.788
THERE’S NO REASON WHY WE CAN’T

00:04:56.789 --> 00:04:58.670
HAVE NUMBER FIVE, SIX, AND SEVEN

00:04:58.672 --> 00:05:01.121
AS WE NEED TO DEAL WITH ISSUES

00:05:01.122 --> 00:05:03.396
THAT OBVIOUSLY ANYTHING WE DO WE

00:05:03.430 --> 00:05:04.511
NEED BIPARTISAN SUPPORT.

00:05:04.546 --> 00:05:06.186
BUT AS IT RELATES TO

00:05:06.187 --> 00:05:08.105
UNEMPLOYMENT INSURANCE, WE KNEW

00:05:08.107 --> 00:05:10.358
THERE WAS GOING TO BE LARGE

00:05:10.359 --> 00:05:10.614
UNEMPLOYMENT.

00:05:10.648 --> 00:05:11.837
WE HAD A TECHNICAL ISSUE WITH

00:05:11.871 --> 00:05:12.952
THE STATES AND HOW THEY WERE

00:05:12.953 --> 00:05:14.865
GOING TO BE ABLE TO DO THIS

00:05:14.866 --> 00:05:18.270
NUMBER SO WE PICKED A NUMBER

00:05:18.304 --> 00:05:20.030
THAT ON THE AVERAGE LOOKED OKAY,

00:05:20.064 --> 00:05:22.230
BUT WHAT WE’VE SEEN IS NOW THAT

00:05:22.231 --> 00:05:23.672
WE WANT TO HAVE THE TECHNICAL

00:05:23.674 --> 00:05:26.065
CORRECTION AND WE WANT TO HAVE

00:05:26.066 --> 00:05:27.142
SOMETHING WHICH PAYS PEOPLE

00:05:27.176 --> 00:05:28.488
ABOUT 70% WAGE REPLACEMENT,

00:05:28.522 --> 00:05:31.307
WHICH I THINK IS A VERY FAIR

00:05:31.309 --> 00:05:32.998
LEVEL, SO IT’S NOT A FIXED

00:05:32.999 --> 00:05:34.169
NUMBER, IT’S SOMETHING THAT PAYS

00:05:34.170 --> 00:05:35.237
YOU A PERCENTAGE OF YOUR WAGES

00:05:35.238 --> 00:05:35.990
THAT ARE LOST.

00:05:36.024 --> 00:05:37.752
AND LET ME JUST SAY, LAST TIME

00:05:37.754 --> 00:05:40.358
PEOPLE THOUGHT WE WOULD HAVE 40

00:05:40.393 --> 00:05:42.051
OR 50 MILLION PEOPLE UNEMPLOYED,

00:05:42.052 --> 00:05:44.504
THE GOOD NEWS IS WE NEVER GOT

00:05:44.538 --> 00:05:45.734
ANYTHING LIKE THAT AND

00:05:45.769 --> 00:05:47.324
MATTER-OF-FACT WHICH CREATED AND

00:05:47.359 --> 00:05:48.717
BROUGHT BACK AN ENORMOUS NUMBER

00:05:48.751 --> 00:05:51.035
OF JOBS, SO ALL THESE DIFFERENT

00:05:51.037 --> 00:05:52.598
PIECES HAVE TO WORK TOGETHER.

00:05:52.599 --> 00:05:53.475
THE PAYCHECK PROTECTION PROGRAM,

00:05:53.476 --> 00:05:55.131
OR WHETHER IT’S THE DIRECT

00:05:55.133 --> 00:05:56.595
PAYMENTS WE SEND OR WHETHER IT’S

00:05:56.596 --> 00:06:00.019
THE MONEY TO SCHOOLS, ALL THIS

00:06:00.020 --> 00:06:02.029
WORKS TOGETHER, SO IT’S JUST A

00:06:02.030 --> 00:06:03.332
COMPONENT OF THE OVERALL

00:06:03.367 --> 00:06:04.625
ECONOMIC PACKAGE, WHICH

00:06:04.659 --> 00:06:06.273
EVERYBODY WANTS THE SAME THING,

00:06:06.274 --> 00:06:08.549
WHICH IS, LET’S GET KIDS BACK TO

00:06:08.584 --> 00:06:11.166
SCHOOL WHERE IT’S SAFE AND LET’S

00:06:11.201 --> 00:06:13.007
GET WORKERS BACK TO THEIR JOBS.

00:06:13.008 --> 00:06:14.535
&gt;&gt; Chris: WHEN I DID MY

00:06:14.536 --> 00:06:15.697
INTERVIEW WITH PRESIDENT TRUMP

00:06:15.698 --> 00:06:18.799
LAST WEEK HE SAID THAT HE MIGHT

00:06:18.800 --> 00:06:22.022
VETO A BILL THAT DID NOT INCLUDE

00:06:22.057 --> 00:06:23.729
A PAYROLL TAX CUT.

00:06:23.763 --> 00:06:26.463
THAT NOW HAS GONE FROM ALL THE

00:06:26.464 --> 00:06:26.695
DISCUSSIONS.

00:06:26.729 --> 00:06:28.526
WHY DO THE ADMINISTRATION CAVE

00:06:28.527 --> 00:06:30.105
ON THAT SO QUICKLY?

00:06:30.139 --> 00:06:31.076
&gt;&gt; Secretary Mnuchin: WELL,

00:06:31.110 --> 00:06:32.059
AND OUR CONVERSATIONS WITH

00:06:32.093 --> 00:06:33.107
PELOSI AND SCHUMER, IT WAS VERY

00:06:33.108 --> 00:06:35.128
CLEAR THAT THE DEMOCRATS WERE

00:06:35.163 --> 00:06:37.279
NOT GOING TO GIVE US A PAYROLL

00:06:37.314 --> 00:06:38.472
TAX CUT, SO THAT’S SOMETHING THE

00:06:38.506 --> 00:06:40.374
PRESIDENT WILL COME BACK AND

00:06:40.408 --> 00:06:42.863
LOOK AT LATER IN THE YEAR --

00:06:42.864 --> 00:06:45.261
&gt;&gt; Chris: BUT SIR, IN

00:06:45.295 --> 00:06:46.558
FAIRNESS, IF I MAY, JUST

00:06:46.559 --> 00:06:47.514
BRIEFLY, IT WASN’T JUST

00:06:47.548 --> 00:06:49.333
DEMOCRATS, THERE WERE A NUMBER

00:06:49.334 --> 00:06:50.234
OF REPUBLICANS WHO REJECTED

00:06:50.235 --> 00:06:50.944
THIS.

00:06:50.945 --> 00:06:53.897
I WANT TO PUT THEM UP ON THE

00:06:53.932 --> 00:06:54.132
SCREEN.

00:06:54.166 --> 00:06:55.394
I’M OF THE TOP REPUBLICAN

00:06:55.395 --> 00:06:56.523
LEADERS IN THE SENATE.

00:06:56.524 --> 00:06:58.274
JOHN THUNE, JOHN CORNYN,

00:06:58.309 --> 00:07:00.422
CHUCK GRASSLEY, THEY ALL SAID

00:07:00.456 --> 00:07:02.068
THEY HAD NO INTEREST IN THAT AS

00:07:02.069 --> 00:07:03.687
WELL, SO YOU GOT BLOWBACK NOT

00:07:03.688 --> 00:07:05.804
JUST FROM DEMOCRATS, BUT FROM

00:07:05.806 --> 00:07:07.004
SOME TOP REPUBLICANS AS WELL.

00:07:07.038 --> 00:07:08.112
&gt;&gt; Secretary Mnuchin: THERE

00:07:08.146 --> 00:07:09.188
ARE OTHER REPUBLICANS THAT

00:07:09.189 --> 00:07:10.376
SUPPORTED IT AND LET ME JUST SAY

00:07:10.378 --> 00:07:12.371
AGAIN, WE KNOW WE NEED

00:07:12.372 --> 00:07:12.916
BIPARTISAN SUPPORT.

00:07:12.917 --> 00:07:15.490
WE HAVE TAX CREDITS THAT WE PUT

00:07:15.524 --> 00:07:16.701
IN HERE TO INCENTIVIZE PEOPLE TO

00:07:16.703 --> 00:07:18.507
GET BACK TO WORK AND SMALL

00:07:18.542 --> 00:07:22.126
BUSINESSES TO HIRE PEOPLE.

00:07:22.127 --> 00:07:24.430
WE HAVE THE DIRECT PAYMENTS AND

00:07:24.431 --> 00:07:25.667
AS YOU KNOW, THE DIRECT PAYMENTS

00:07:25.669 --> 00:07:26.536
ARE MUCH QUICKER WAY OF

00:07:26.537 --> 00:07:27.535
EFFECTIVELY GIVING EVERYBODY A

00:07:27.537 --> 00:07:31.117
TAX CUT AND IT’S MUCH QUICKER

00:07:31.151 --> 00:07:33.289
THAN THE PAYROLL TAX CUT.

00:07:33.323 --> 00:07:35.103
&gt;&gt; Chris: MEANWHILE, 32 -- YOU

00:07:35.104 --> 00:07:36.471
SAY WE DON’T HAVE 40 MILLION

00:07:36.472 --> 00:07:38.772
UNEMPLOYED, WE DO HAVE

00:07:38.806 --> 00:07:40.901
32 MILLION PEOPLE UNEMPLOYED AND

00:07:40.935 --> 00:07:44.910
MORE PEOPLE APPLIED FOR JOBLESS

00:07:44.911 --> 00:07:46.107
BENEFITS LAST WEEK.

00:07:46.142 --> 00:07:47.565
1.4 MILLION THAT HAD APPLIED THE

00:07:47.599 --> 00:07:50.417
WEEK BEFORE, SO NO ONE

00:07:50.451 --> 00:07:52.016
APPOINTMENT IS GOING UP, NOT

00:07:52.050 --> 00:07:52.410
DOWN.

00:07:52.411 --> 00:07:54.725
MEANWHILE, WE ARE SEEING THIS

00:07:54.727 --> 00:07:57.112
SEARCH IN THE VIRUS AND MORE AND

00:07:57.146 --> 00:08:00.011
MORE STATES ARE THE DELAYING OR

00:08:00.045 --> 00:08:02.024
ACTUALLY ROLLING BACK SOME OF

00:08:02.025 --> 00:08:02.462
THEIR REOPENING’S.

00:08:02.463 --> 00:08:05.125
ISN’T THIS GOING TO HAVE AN

00:08:05.127 --> 00:08:06.658
EFFECT ON THE RECOVERY AND IS

00:08:06.659 --> 00:08:08.798
THERE A POSSIBILITY OF A DOUBLE

00:08:08.832 --> 00:08:09.270
DIP RECESSION?

00:08:09.271 --> 00:08:10.265
&gt;&gt; Secretary Mnuchin: LET ME

00:08:10.266 --> 00:08:12.740
JUST POINT OUT, AS YOU SAID, WE

00:08:12.775 --> 00:08:14.860
GOT TO 30, WE NEVER GOT TO 40 OR

00:08:14.894 --> 00:08:17.054
50, THAT’S A HUGE DIFFERENCE IN

00:08:17.055 --> 00:08:18.786
WE’VE CREATED ALMOST 10 MILLION

00:08:18.787 --> 00:08:20.641
JOBS IN STENCIL WHAT WE ARE IN A

